--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 78c39ca0aa3b4c60ad7cb11e9f4cf262, type: 3}
  m_Name: TutorialTopic_Towns
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Features.Tutorial.Data.TutorialTopicData
  <Title>k__BackingField: Towns
  <Chapters>k__BackingField:
  - <Title>k__BackingField: General
    <Description>k__BackingField: Towns are your way of winning games. You will trade
      with them, get them on your side, complete their missions and help them develop
      and prosper.
    <Image>k__BackingField: {fileID: 2800000, guid: f98f770fb6e4dec4482fbe90558c34d0, type: 3}
  - <Title>k__BackingField: Development
    <Description>k__BackingField: 'Each town has a development gauge that reflects
      its growth over time. Supplying foreign goods, completing missions and building
      production increases the towns development trend.

      With growing development
      more and more development milestones unlock, improving the towns stats and
      enabling further trade opportunities.'
    <Image>k__BackingField: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 65dc82cb32e094343af93995340cd60b, type: 3}
  - <Title>k__BackingField: Missions
    <Description>k__BackingField: Towns will occasionally start trade missions where
      they request specific goods. Fulfilling these requests will aid their development.
      Failing to supply requested goods in time will set the town back however.
    <Image>k__BackingField: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 7dfecc8add197ff4387bdfb6cf0ebf06, type: 3}
  - <Title>k__BackingField: Advancing Town Tiers
    <Description>k__BackingField: 'To help a town advance to the next tier, you must
      complete its upgrade missions. These become available once the town reaches
      a development of 100.

      Towns of higher tiers can produce higher tier
      goods which usually have better margins for you.'
    <Image>k__BackingField: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 2e679e68766b46b479ba9da6d893fc18, type: 3}
  - <Title>k__BackingField: Reputation
    <Description>k__BackingField: 'Towns remember how you treat them. Their opinion
      of you changes with each trade and as you help them develop or choose to neglect
      them.

      Trades, constuction of buildings, failing or completing missions,
      among others all influence your reputation with towns.'
    <Image>k__BackingField: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 3f6c70e54ab649749a3a8ebbc3f2bdbf, type: 3}
  - <Title>k__BackingField: Production Buildings
    <Description>k__BackingField: 'You can finance production buildings in towns
      to make them produce goods and raise development.

      Constructing producers
      is essential as they add more resources to your trade network and enable you
      to complete missions, react to world events and make profits by supplying the
      right goods at the right time.'
    <Image>k__BackingField: {fileID: 2800000, guid: c383bf2cacf907545a33bd17c325868f, type: 3}
  - <Title>k__BackingField: Producer Tiers
    <Description>k__BackingField: 'Tier I buildings can be built based on the towns
      neighboring regions.

      Tier II buildings are built on top of Tier I buildings.

      Tier
      III buildings are built on top of a Tier II producer and require a seconds
      Tier II good to produce Tier III goods. This second good can either be produced
      in the town or must be delivered (sold) by you.'
    <Image>k__BackingField: {fileID: 2800000, guid: c0a77cebe55681e418b4dd17db294ec3, type: 3}
